<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2">
  <Document>
    <name>🌡️ LIVE AIR TEMPERATURE</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<h2>LIVE AIR TEMPERATURE</h2><p><b>Gradient key</b><br><img src="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/air_temperature/legend.png" width="600" alt="gradient key"><br>2 m air temperature (degF), fixed Apple-style absolute spectrum (-40..130 F): purple extreme cold → blue → cyan → green → yellow → orange → red extreme heat. Same temperature always shows the same color. Record <b>LOWEST 27.11</b> / <b>HIGHEST+ 77.12</b> marked on the scale. Freezing has no color break.</p><p>This entry auto-refreshes from the live overlay (source: NOAA/NCEP HRRR 3 km 2 m temperature analysis, hourly cycles).<br/><b>Data time:</b> 2026-09-25 03:00 PM EDT<br/><b>Source version:</b> hrrr-hrrr.20260925-t19z<br/><b>Status:</b> LIVE / CURRENT MODEL (analysis)</p><p>Turn on/off independently of all other layers. Add this file once; new source cycles appear automatically.</p><p><i>Not endorsed by NOAA.</i></p>]]></description>
    <NetworkLink>
      <name>🌡️ LIVE AIR TEMPERATURE — auto-refresh</name>
      <Link>
        <href>https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/kml/live/Great_Lakes_Live_Air_Temperature.kml</href>
        <refreshMode>onInterval</refreshMode>
        <refreshInterval>3600</refreshInterval>
      </Link>
    </NetworkLink>
  </Document>
